# tab_side_info

**Claim carried:** C6: gains from side information X credited to calibration only if they exceed the linear-with-X arm.

**Shows:** E6, T2 arms (f and X), one block per dataset and n: mean width, coverage with Wilson 95% CI, paired width ratio to the PPI++ arm that uses f only, on the same draws (longtable); bold = shortest valid width; Floor with X is a model-based prediction (no coverage, no paired CI); dagger = coverage fails the win rule.

**How to read:** a gain from X is credited to calibration only if the calibrated +X row (B3) or the selected row (B5) is shorter than the vector PPI++ and OLS-adjusted rows at valid coverage; a ratio at or above 1 means no gain over f-only PPI++.

